{
  "_": "Activity sessions (ADR 0008): computed in memory from activity captures, never stored. Every implementation gives these answers; the reference (src/sessions.js) and the macOS daemon both test against this file. Activity is captured only when something changes, so each capture lasts until the next (the last until now). A session is a run of active time in one app and window, or in excluded windows, which have neither. A run of other active captures lasting under 30 seconds in all, after which the person is back in the same app and window, doesn't end the session: it's taken into it. Idle (no input for two minutes, as the capturer decides) and locked time end a session and belong to none. A session's id is 'ses_' and the id of its first capture; ended_at is when the capture that ended it began, or null while it goes on.",
